t `decode_hex`/`decode_base64`, byte-or-text argument reader, the eight runtime arms, a fallible `uuid.generate`, and UTF-8-aware base64 error text | | `tests/encoding_hashing_test.rs` | new, 279 lines / 9 tests | round trips, padding, literal digests, UUID formats, strict-error positions, Unicode, type and range refusals | | `tests/libraries_policy_test.rs` | +25 −20 | phase-094's refusal probe now records that `base64.decode` landed while the open `percent.encode` binding is still refused as unknown | | `tests/stdlib_module_names_test.rs` | +20 | exercise the four new modules in the documents-vs-registry sweep | | `tests/stdlib_module_docs_test.rs` | +42 | each of the eight new builtins now has a program and an expected output | | `tests/doc_blocks_runs.txt` | +10 −7 | classify the three new SPEC examples, re-anchor the shifted SPEC line numbers, and refresh the bucket counts | | `SPEC.md` | +49 | document `hex`, `base64`, `hash` and `uuid`, including the raise-vs-sentinel rule | | `README.md` | +17 | quick reference for the four new modules | | `LIBRARIES.md` | +5 | record that the encodings/digests row is now bound; `percent-encoding` stays open | | `SURVEY.md` | +37 −35 | rank 8 records phase-104 closing the encoding, digest and UUID gaps; counts and citations re-anchored |  ## Tests added  | Test | Edge class covered | |---|---| | `edge_hex_and_base64_round_trip_all_256_byte_values` | boundary / all 256 byte values, asserted on the byte list | | `edge_base64_uses_canonical_padding_and_decodes_padded_or_unpadded` | empty, singleton, padding and unpadded input, literal expected text | | `edge_hex_single_byte_empty_and_uppercase_inputs` | empty, singleton, `0x00`/`0xff`, uppercase input | | `edge_invalid_hex_and_base64_name_the_offending_position` | malformed input, whitespace, wrong hex length, invalid base64 symbol | | `edge_decoding_errors_are_catchable` | asserts a failure is produced and caught by `try … catch error of Runtime` | | `edge_hashes_match_literal