 | |---|---| | `cargo fmt --all -- --check` | pass — exit 0, no diff | | `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` | pass — exit 0, no warnings | | `cargo test --all-targets` | pass — **2527 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored** across 80 test binaries | | `../rbops/verify.sh phase-104` | pass — `VERIFY PASS — phase-104` |  The full run was executed locally with cargo; `verify.sh` then re-ran the four gates and the example sweep. No gate was skipped, relaxed or weakened, and no `#[ignore]`, `// skip` or `allow(clippy::` suppression was added.  This checkout is uncommitted, so the local verify used a copy of the index (`GIT_INDEX_FILE=target/tmp/phase104_index`) as phase-094 did. Without it the `git add -N` that `verify.sh` performs is undone while `cargo test` runs, and the gate reads 0 new tests on an untracked test file. The pipeline commits the phase before verifying, where the same diff is ordinary. No check was skipped.  ## Invariants touched  - **None.** No `Value` variant, `Error` variant, grammar production, `.rb`   extension, `to … end` / `set x to …` / `say` form, trailing-comma rule or   `{interp}` behaviour changed. The existing `bytes` module is unchanged and   its tests pass unmodified.  ## Known gaps / follow-ups  - `percent-encoding` (the fourth crate in the LIBRARIES.md encodings row) is not   bound; it remains an open entry rather than pretending rank 8 is completely   closed. - `hash` exposes SHA-256 and SHA-512 only; SHA-1, MD5 and keyed digests (HMAC)   are not added, because the policy requires audited primitives and nothing in   this phase's finding asked for them. - `uuid.generate` generates version 4 only; name-based and time-based UUIDs are   not exposed. - The WebAssembly target is not built by these gates. `uuid` needs its   `getrandom` wasm feature if the playground build is ever extended to call   `uuid.generate`; that belongs to the wasm build phase, not this one.  ```
